WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Mount Everest stands at 8,848 meters above sea level, the highest point on Earth.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.500
It is located in the Himalayan mountain range on the border between Nepal and Tibet.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The first successful ascent was made by Sir Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay in 1953.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.500
Since then, thousands of climbers have attempted the summit, with varying degrees of success.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
The climb requires months of preparation and carries significant risks at extreme altitudes.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.000
Despite the dangers, the mountain continues to draw adventurers from every corner of the globe.

